The constant-store replacements write 42 where the source wrote true, and a
bool occupies a byte, in which 42 is still true: on the tree this was written
against seven such stores survived, each a mutant no test can tell from the
program. A store or an initialisation whose value is the literal true is not a
mutation site; one whose value is false keeps its mutant, since 42 there is a
flag set the other way.
